# Lex Fridman Podcast Semantic RAG Pipeline: AGI Timelines Analysis

An end-to-end Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) application built with [LangChain](https://www.langchain.com/) and [FAISS](https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss). This pipeline queries a vector database of Lex Fridman podcast transcripts to synthesize expert predictions on complex topics like Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) timelines.

## Project Overview

1. **Knowledge Retrieval (`FAISS`)**: Loads a local vector store containing pre-embedded podcast transcripts. When a query (e.g., *"What are predicted timelines for AGI?"*) is submitted, it performs a semantic similarity search to pull the top $k=10$ most relevant transcript chunks.
2. **Prompt Engineering (`PromptTemplate`)**: Formats the retrieved context and user question into an expert analyst framework defined in `prompt.md`, instructing the LLM to group viewpoints, provide direct quotes, and maintain strict source attribution.
3. **Response Generation (`ChatModel`)**: Combines retrieval and generation using LangChain Expression Language (LCEL) (`semantic_rag = retrieve_knowledge | generate_response`) to generate structured, balanced perspectives.

